            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "C. Stand-by duty shall mean that a department head has ordered any employee to be immediately available for duty upon receipt of a message to report to work. If any employee assigned to stand-by duty is not available to report to duty when called, no stand-by pay shall be paid to the employee for the period.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                291,
                1084,
                415
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 1,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    291.0
                ],
                [
                    1084.0,
                    291.0
                ],
                [
                    1084.0,
                    415.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    415.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "D. Should a department head require coverage of a work location on a 24-hour basis, such department head will establish a list of employees to be available for duty. The least senior employee in the work location shall be first on the list. Having once been put on stand-by duty, the next junior employee will be placed on stand-by duty, etc. With the approval of the department, employees may substitute for one another under this Section.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                446,
                1084,
                629
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    136.0,
                    446.0
                ],
                [
                    1084.0,
                    446.0
                ],
                [
                    1084.0,
                    629.0
                ],
                [
                    136.0,
                    629.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "E. Stand-by duty shall be voluntary except in the case of an emergency. There shall be no discrimination or discipline taken against any employee who declines stand-by in a non-emergency situation. Should no volunteer be available and the department head determines that an emergency exists, the department head will assign an employee to such stand-by duty.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                661,
                1083,
                815
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    137.0,
                    669.0
                ],
                [
                    1082.0,
                    669.0
                ],
                [
                    1082.0,
                    814.0
                ],
                [
                    137.0,
                    814.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "F. When the practice has been for the Employer to provide the employees on stand-by with a beeper, this practice shall continue.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                845,
                1082,
